      "body": "### Motivation\n\nWhen passing longer videos to MiMo v2.6, timestamps were generated as  where  was hardcoded.\nSince video loaders uniformly sample frames across the duration of the clip (e.g. 32 frames), every video received timestamps labelled  regardless of its actual length, leading to incorrect timestamp reporting and prompt slicing.\n\nFixes #65523.\n\n### Proposed Changes\n\nIn :\n- Respect  from  or the video metadata/object attribute when available, falling back to .\n- When  are present in metadata, use  to reflect true sampled timestamps.\n- If explicit timestamps are provided on the input, preserve them.\n",
